WEBVTT

00:00:02.290 --> 00:00:04.500
APOLOGY FOR DISOBEYING ORDERS
NAME: DAISUKE DOJIMA

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:07.090
<i>That day, that time,</i>

00:00:08.250 --> 00:00:10.260
<i>the people who saved me
when I was kidnapped were</i>

00:00:11.050 --> 00:00:13.800
<i>Lu, Marimari, Keisaku, Gai,</i>

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:16.470
<i>and Milo.</i>

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:18.560
Thank you!

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:20.310
Thank you, miss.

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:24.980
Listen to me, Daisuke. This is a prophecy.

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:29.360
The five of you will someday
find yourselves in terrible danger.

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.650
Only you will be able to protect them.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:37.570
<i>That was when Milo told me my destiny
to protect everyone.</i>

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:39.870
<i>I believed it that day.</i>

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:41.870
<i>I've always believed it.</i>

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:43.410
<i>But...</i>

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:46.750
Take a hint!
Your heroic antics are annoying!

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:48.840
You need to stop it with your delusions.

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:51.090
You'll go crazy, you'll be a nutcase!

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:52.510
<i>You're going too far.</i>

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:54.840
<i>My friends who were there</i>

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:58.010
<i>didn't believe that
what Milo said was true.</i>

00:00:58.640 --> 00:00:59.560
<i>But I did.</i>

00:01:00.970 --> 00:01:03.730
<i>In middle school, I was supposed to
move away with my parents,</i>

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:06.770
<i>but I insisted on living with my uncle,
so I could stay.</i>

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:09.150
<i>That's because I believed Milo's prophecy.</i>

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:10.520
<i>But</i>

00:01:10.610 --> 00:01:14.190
<i>even after I became a high school student,
"that time" never came,</i>

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:16.990
<i>so I was always...</i>

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:56.880
<i>Let me out, damn it!</i>

00:02:56.960 --> 00:02:59.590
How long are you going to keep me in here?

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:01.180
-Hey, Daisuke.
-Goddamn it!

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:02.470
-Hey!
-Keep it down.

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:03.470
What's the deal?

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:05.140
I think you know.

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:06.520
Don't you think this is nuts?

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:09.770
We're the ones protecting Shibuya,
so why are we in jail?

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:11.810
Okay.

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:13.980
Just keep it down, all right?

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:15.940
<i>That's right.</i>

00:03:16.690 --> 00:03:18.440
<i>The reason I'm here</i>

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:22.910
<i>is because the world changed that day.</i>

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:26.660
<i>The world was transformed in that moment</i>

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:28.160
<i>like Milo said it would.</i>

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:32.420
<i>But I couldn't do a thing.</i>

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:33.670
<i>I thought I was ready.</i>

00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:38.210
<i>The person who saved me</i>

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:40.010
<i>was Milo, of course.</i>

00:03:41.260 --> 00:03:42.470
<i>When I met Milo again,</i>

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:45.720
<i>she gave me the power
of the String Puppet.</i>

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:49.520
<i>It was power that was destined
to be mine alone.</i>

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:51.390
<i>That's why I fought.</i>

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:52.980
<i>For everyone's sake.</i>

00:03:58.150 --> 00:03:59.570
<i>That's right!</i>

00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:01.070
<i>It's because I've worked so hard</i>

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:04.570
<i>and believed.
That's why everyone has survived.</i>

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:07.660
<i>Then why the hell is this happening,
goddamn it?</i>

00:04:09.620 --> 00:04:11.870
This is a perfect example of what I mean.

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:15.670
Do you think everything revolves
around you?

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:16.590
Don't be ridiculous!

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:19.880
Let go of me! I'm the leader!

00:04:20.050 --> 00:04:20.960
There you go again.

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:22.380
Because I am!

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:24.890
It doesn't matter which of you
is the leader!

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:28.180
Why does this have to happen?

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:31.140
I thought our friendship returned
to how it was before.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:32.430
Why?

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:39.820
I can't believe you are worth
my friends and family risking their lives

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:41.530
to protect you.

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:53.160
What? You still haven't written it?

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:56.290
I didn't know why I had to write
an apology either.

00:04:56.540 --> 00:04:58.960
Why should I be thrown in jail
just for going out

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:00.380
to look for my mother?

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:02.090
And then...

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:06.720
Well, once I started writing, it was easy.

00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:08.260
Is that so?

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:11.140
Daisuke, you're way too stubborn.

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:13.390
You need to grow up a little.

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:16.390
If you don't hurry up
and accept reality and get on with life,

00:05:16.850 --> 00:05:18.650
you'll take important stuff for granted.

00:05:19.730 --> 00:05:21.530
What kind of important stuff?

00:05:23.150 --> 00:05:24.990
Never mind. Forget I said anything.

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:27.660
What?

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:30.620
Down with government oppression!

00:05:30.870 --> 00:05:32.040
Down with oppression!

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:37.000
Let's see. We are presently
quietly moving ahead with the plan

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:40.090
and making progress as fast as possible...

00:05:42.460 --> 00:05:45.470
You people are clueless!
Mayor Muta's ego trip

00:05:45.550 --> 00:05:49.140
and the rampage those kids went on
are all your fault!

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:51.850
Rampage?
Don't you think that's going too far?

00:05:52.220 --> 00:05:54.220
It's not like we're fighting
because we want to!

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:55.270
Sit down, Lu.

00:05:55.350 --> 00:05:58.900
If we hadn't fought back,
more people would have been

00:05:59.020 --> 00:06:00.440
dragged away by the Revisions.

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:01.650
Lu!

00:06:01.820 --> 00:06:02.690
You,

00:06:02.980 --> 00:06:05.690
why don't you come work at one of
my establishments after you graduate?

00:06:06.110 --> 00:06:10.280
I'll give you special training in
what you need to be a popular hostess.

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:11.870
-What?
-Mr. Yokoyama,

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:15.410
I don't approve of you
talking like that to minors.

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:16.500
Dr. Dojima,

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:18.710
I realize you've helped me out,

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:20.750
but this and that are different matters!

00:06:21.420 --> 00:06:23.590
It was your nephew
who went on that rampage!

00:06:24.130 --> 00:06:26.380
Why don't you
quit trying to change the subject?

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:27.510
At any rate,

00:06:27.970 --> 00:06:31.090
the government must take responsibility
for relying on these kids on everything!

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:33.510
So, do you have any concrete suggestions?

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:35.520
I've been telling you from the start!

00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:38.390
We need to get back to our original time!

00:06:38.480 --> 00:06:40.940
I agree with you on that.

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:44.360
Milo,

00:06:44.690 --> 00:06:47.070
I think it's about time
you told us everything you know.

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:49.740
We can't keep fighting in this situation.

00:06:52.240 --> 00:06:54.200
Goddamn person of the future.

00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:56.490
All right.

00:06:57.830 --> 00:07:02.000
I will tell you everything
that only the higher-ups know.

00:07:02.630 --> 00:07:05.960
We kept silent
to avoid confusing the public,

00:07:06.050 --> 00:07:08.670
but it appears
that we can't keep silent anymore.

00:07:08.760 --> 00:07:11.380
Milo, I want you to confirm
this following information if you can.

00:07:11.470 --> 00:07:12.720
First of all, the Revisions

00:07:12.840 --> 00:07:16.100
are people infected with the RV virus
who came down with the disease.

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:18.310
The disease

00:07:18.850 --> 00:07:23.770
<i>bloats the body, atrophies the brain,
and eventually leads to death.</i>

00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:25.110
Is that correct?

00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:26.900
Yes.

00:07:26.980 --> 00:07:28.490
You mean to tell me

00:07:28.570 --> 00:07:30.860
<i>those monsters are humans like us?</i>

00:07:35.030 --> 00:07:38.330
But the Revisions
who we were negotiating with

00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:41.080
had the same form
as the rest of us, humans.

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:43.170
<i>That's what we call
a remote communication body.</i>

00:07:43.630 --> 00:07:47.050
<i>It's a temporary form.
Their real body is elsewhere.</i>

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:50.470
For the Revisions to curb the disease,

00:07:50.550 --> 00:07:52.880
they need the cells of normal humans.

00:07:52.970 --> 00:07:54.090
Yes, that's right.

00:07:54.970 --> 00:07:58.600
<i>To fight against them,
the String Puppets were made.</i>

00:07:59.060 --> 00:08:00.060
<i>Isn't that right?</i>

00:08:00.230 --> 00:08:03.060
<i>With the disintegration of the country
and the lack of a real army,</i>

00:08:03.480 --> 00:08:04.940
<i>they are humanity's only hope.</i>

00:08:05.440 --> 00:08:09.440
And the only people who can pilot
the String Puppets are the members of SDS.

00:08:09.820 --> 00:08:10.900
Why is that?

00:08:10.990 --> 00:08:13.200
To prevent the Revisions from using them.

00:08:14.030 --> 00:08:17.450
<i>The machine links with the pilot
via cerebral nerve mapping.</i>

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:21.960
<i>Who determined that Daisuke
and the others would be the pilots?</i>

00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:23.870
<i>This is only a guess,</i>

00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:27.750
<i>but when I leaped to 2010,
I determined they were suitable candidates</i>

00:08:28.460 --> 00:08:29.960
<i>and saved their data.</i>

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:33.090
<i>The instructions I received </i>

00:08:33.590 --> 00:08:37.260
<i>were based on the fact that
Keisaku, Gai, Lu, Temari, and Daisuke</i>

00:08:37.970 --> 00:08:40.930
<i>are the ones
that the String Puppets were tuned for.</i>

00:08:41.560 --> 00:08:42.480
<i>Then that means</i>

00:08:43.020 --> 00:08:46.440
<i>AHRV developed the String Puppets
even though they can't use them</i>

00:08:47.060 --> 00:08:48.650
<i>and our forced leap to the future</i>

00:08:48.770 --> 00:08:50.900
<i>was already anticipated. Isn't that right?</i>

00:08:50.980 --> 00:08:52.490
<i>Yes, that's right.</i>

00:08:52.610 --> 00:08:56.910
<i>So, you intentionally didn't stop them
from transporting Shibuya.</i>

00:08:57.030 --> 00:09:00.450
<i>You had them pilot the String Puppets
because you had to collect data on them.</i>

00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:02.410
-Isn't that right?
-Yes.

00:09:02.500 --> 00:09:03.580
"Yes"? Why, you--

00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:07.080
How cruel! You mean we were guinea pigs?

00:09:07.170 --> 00:09:09.090
However, thanks to the String Puppets,

00:09:09.210 --> 00:09:11.090
Shibuya was saved. Isn't that right?

00:09:11.170 --> 00:09:12.260
What?

00:09:12.510 --> 00:09:16.050
But you let us be transported
into the future, right?

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:17.390
Gai!

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:20.310
Let's go, Marimari.

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:23.730
Can you follow them, Keisaku?

00:09:23.810 --> 00:09:25.060
Sure.

00:09:32.110 --> 00:09:34.490
Everyone, shout clear and loud!

00:09:35.110 --> 00:09:37.160
I haven't said anything until now,

00:09:37.950 --> 00:09:39.620
but if all AHRV wanted was data,

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:42.950
then weren't they planning on
abandoning us from the start?

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:44.160
No, that's not true.

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:47.580
With the data from the String Puppets,
mass production would be possible

00:09:47.870 --> 00:09:49.460
and we could fight against the Revisions.

00:09:50.170 --> 00:09:52.250
If their artificial quantum brain
can be destroyed,

00:09:52.710 --> 00:09:54.960
then Shibuya should be able to
return to 2017.

00:09:55.470 --> 00:09:56.930
Then what are your concrete--

00:09:57.010 --> 00:09:59.140
Have you begun mass production
of the String Puppets?

00:09:59.890 --> 00:10:01.140
When will you attack their base?

00:10:01.720 --> 00:10:02.720
Well...

00:10:03.430 --> 00:10:06.350
You don't know?
Or are you hiding something?

00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:08.140
You have a responsibility to explain!

00:10:08.270 --> 00:10:09.310
You useless woman!

00:10:11.150 --> 00:10:12.770
Mr. Yokoyama, that's enough!

00:10:13.230 --> 00:10:15.440
She is our only connection to AHRV!

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:18.360
-But don't you see--
-Haven't you figured it out yet?

00:10:19.110 --> 00:10:20.280
Our interests are not

00:10:20.370 --> 00:10:23.790
completely aligned with AHRV's,
let alone the Revisions'.

00:10:23.870 --> 00:10:27.870
That means we have no choice
but to stand up for ourselves.

00:10:29.460 --> 00:10:30.420
Mr. Yokoyama,

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:33.500
I leave the explanation to local councils
and the chamber of commerce to you.

00:10:34.050 --> 00:10:35.880
But avoid causing a panic.

00:10:39.130 --> 00:10:40.590
Logically, I understand this.

00:10:40.720 --> 00:10:42.970
But what about people's emotions?

00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:46.680
The temporary government
and SDS get special treatment.

00:10:46.770 --> 00:10:49.600
<i>They can use all the electricity
and water they want.</i>

00:10:49.690 --> 00:10:51.020
<i>The same goes with food!</i>

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:56.280
The women at my establishments
are working even in these times.

00:10:56.990 --> 00:10:57.820
Why is that?

00:10:57.900 --> 00:11:01.780
Because what you're doing isn't enough
to satisfy everyone! Do you understand?

00:11:02.410 --> 00:11:05.330
I bet you think you're the only ones
fighting to help us!

00:11:05.410 --> 00:11:07.620
Quit acting like the guardians of justice!

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:10.330
Look at reality!
See what's right at your feet!

00:11:12.920 --> 00:11:17.050
Finally, everything necessary to construct
my new body has been assembled.

00:11:17.130 --> 00:11:19.170
But that won't cure the disease.

00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:23.180
As long as I am myself,
I must live with the disease.

00:11:23.850 --> 00:11:26.260
But it will be different
than this artificial thing.

00:11:26.930 --> 00:11:31.480
I'll get a real physical body,
raw flesh that has a quantum brain.

00:11:32.100 --> 00:11:34.650
I will still be in this body,

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:37.900
however, I will have a body
that can move freely.

00:11:38.030 --> 00:11:40.400
You know, I don't think

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:44.530
this plan will work
unless one of us leaps to 2017.

00:11:44.620 --> 00:11:46.620
What are you talking about?

00:11:46.740 --> 00:11:49.870
How many times have I told you
that while this era and 2017 are

00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:52.710
under simultaneous observation,
we can fix Shibuya here?

00:11:53.420 --> 00:11:55.210
I understand the logic, Mukyu.

00:11:55.420 --> 00:11:57.920
Then, why can't I also leap through time?

00:11:58.500 --> 00:11:59.420
Nicholas,

00:11:59.590 --> 00:12:02.300
considering your position,
you can't have that honor.

00:12:03.720 --> 00:12:06.930
There's not that big of a difference
in our status!

00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:09.770
As I thought, you still don't get it,
little doggy.

00:12:10.270 --> 00:12:13.020
I told you that
there is a greater possibility

00:12:13.140 --> 00:12:15.650
for identical twins like me and Chiharu.

00:12:15.770 --> 00:12:18.230
However, when I get my new body,

00:12:18.360 --> 00:12:19.820
it's farewell to you, Mukyu.

00:12:20.030 --> 00:12:21.820
What are you talking about, Chiharu?

00:12:21.900 --> 00:12:23.450
We're sisters.

00:12:23.740 --> 00:12:26.320
You and I are one no matter where we go.

00:12:26.530 --> 00:12:29.660
The two of us are going to save
the future of humanity.

00:12:29.740 --> 00:12:31.830
Yes. That's right!

00:12:33.830 --> 00:12:35.330
LET ME OUT! THIS IS FALSE IMPRISONMENT!

00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:37.630
Come on, enough already.
Let me out of here.

00:12:37.710 --> 00:12:40.050
Why don't you want
to write the letter of apology?

00:12:40.300 --> 00:12:42.010
The building was destroyed by accident.

00:12:42.510 --> 00:12:44.300
I didn't do anything wrong.

00:12:44.680 --> 00:12:45.930
Quit being so stubborn.

00:12:46.510 --> 00:12:48.600
What happened to all that talk
about your destiny?

00:12:48.850 --> 00:12:50.350
Aren't you going to protect everyone?

00:12:50.430 --> 00:12:51.350
That's why

00:12:51.680 --> 00:12:54.140
Keisaku and I went to search
for the enemy's base.

00:12:54.230 --> 00:12:56.060
Without consulting anyone
or getting permission.

00:12:56.150 --> 00:12:59.110
By defying people
and the society like that,

00:12:59.190 --> 00:13:00.570
-you'll never--
-It's the opposite!

00:13:00.650 --> 00:13:02.650
I'm the one
who's been protecting everybody.

00:13:03.440 --> 00:13:06.410
It's the society and the people
who should apologize to me first.

00:13:06.780 --> 00:13:08.280
But this is how I'm treated instead.

00:13:08.370 --> 00:13:11.200
I told you,
this is just improvised punishment.

00:13:11.450 --> 00:13:12.450
Some people got injured.

00:13:12.540 --> 00:13:14.620
To satisfy them, we need to--

00:13:14.710 --> 00:13:18.960
We don't need to satisfy people who just
sit around letting us protect them!

00:13:20.170 --> 00:13:22.050
Who the hell do you think
you are, Daisuke?

00:13:22.420 --> 00:13:24.510
You don't even try
to fit into society at all.

00:13:24.720 --> 00:13:26.380
You act like a hero
and look down on others.

00:13:26.550 --> 00:13:28.680
You're not the only one piloting
a String Puppet, right?

00:13:28.760 --> 00:13:31.560
But it's thanks to me
that everyone's alive, right?

00:13:32.060 --> 00:13:33.390
Then show some appreciation!

00:13:33.470 --> 00:13:35.230
Say "thank you!"

00:13:35.310 --> 00:13:37.350
Show me some recognition!
I want recognition!

00:13:37.440 --> 00:13:38.860
That's enough!

00:13:39.110 --> 00:13:42.320
Why don't you think about
the reason why no one is grateful?

00:13:42.900 --> 00:13:44.070
Listen to me, Daisuke.

00:13:44.650 --> 00:13:48.320
Even if you boast how great you are,
they won't understand.

00:13:48.990 --> 00:13:51.700
Daisuke, don't you remember
what Marin said?

00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:57.540
If I had known people will get hurt,
I would have done it.

00:13:57.920 --> 00:13:59.630
<i>So tell me to do it, Daisuke.</i>

00:14:00.130 --> 00:14:02.300
<i>Tell me to pilot the String Puppet.</i>

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:07.630
Even Marin, who hated the thought
of piloting a String Puppet,

00:14:08.470 --> 00:14:11.010
she's trying to understand you, you know.

00:14:13.560 --> 00:14:16.520
Carefully. Nice and slow.

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:18.390
Nice.

00:14:18.480 --> 00:14:20.900
Good job!
I knew you could do it, Marimari.

00:14:21.480 --> 00:14:24.780
I think I got the hang of
making little movements.

00:14:28.360 --> 00:14:29.570
I do feel bad about

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:31.820
forcing you guys to do this

00:14:32.530 --> 00:14:34.450
and that I can't show you the way back.

00:14:36.120 --> 00:14:37.120
Say, Milo...

00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:39.420
How old are you? Do you have a family?

00:14:40.460 --> 00:14:42.540
Tell us about yourself, Milo.

00:14:43.290 --> 00:14:44.170
I'm 19.

00:14:44.670 --> 00:14:45.760
My whole family is dead.

00:14:47.510 --> 00:14:48.550
I'm sorry.

00:14:49.180 --> 00:14:50.010
Don't worry about it.

00:14:50.800 --> 00:14:51.720
And you, Marimari?

00:14:51.840 --> 00:14:54.060
Me? Well...

00:14:54.890 --> 00:14:56.600
I have a mother and a father.

00:14:57.270 --> 00:14:59.350
We take trips as a family

00:15:00.100 --> 00:15:01.020
and get along well.

00:15:01.650 --> 00:15:02.810
That must be fun.

00:15:02.900 --> 00:15:03.770
Yes.

00:15:04.650 --> 00:15:07.860
I want to return you to your time.
That's the truth.

00:15:09.360 --> 00:15:10.990
Oh, they're back.

00:15:15.490 --> 00:15:17.450
What do you intend to do with this?

00:15:17.540 --> 00:15:20.160
This will become parts
for the broken String Puppet.

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:22.920
Really?

00:15:23.500 --> 00:15:24.590
As I thought.

00:15:24.960 --> 00:15:27.170
"As I thought"? You knew about this?

00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:29.760
I kind of figured it might be so.

00:15:30.130 --> 00:15:33.760
There's nothing around here.
The only thing that can be used is...

00:15:33.850 --> 00:15:35.720
So, the String Puppets are...

00:15:36.140 --> 00:15:37.100
Civilians.

00:15:37.520 --> 00:15:39.390
That means they're made from people.

00:15:39.480 --> 00:15:40.520
Seriously?

00:15:40.600 --> 00:15:41.480
Yes.

00:15:42.020 --> 00:15:44.610
By dismantling these at the nano-level
and reassembling them,

00:15:44.690 --> 00:15:46.020
the String Puppet can be repaired.

00:15:47.780 --> 00:15:49.740
<i>Are the SDS members around?</i>

00:15:53.820 --> 00:15:55.320
Who is it now?

00:16:02.330 --> 00:16:03.960
How the heck did you get in here?

00:16:04.040 --> 00:16:06.340
What an incredible asshole you are.

00:16:06.460 --> 00:16:09.170
I've come here to talk, so quit shouting.

00:16:11.510 --> 00:16:13.340
You seem down, boy.

00:16:13.590 --> 00:16:15.340
Did buddies abandon you?

00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:17.930
Shut up! What would you know?

00:16:18.010 --> 00:16:21.640
People discriminate against one another
to affirm their position in the world.

00:16:21.770 --> 00:16:25.100
Boy, what are you doing here, anyway?

00:16:25.650 --> 00:16:27.020
Can't you tell, you dog?

00:16:27.400 --> 00:16:30.570
My name is Nicholas.
Well, I'm glad I came.

00:16:31.030 --> 00:16:35.070
Hey, boy, Daisuke is your name, isn't it?
Do you want to join our side?

00:16:35.410 --> 00:16:38.490
-What?
-I mean, you're all alone, aren't you?

00:16:38.740 --> 00:16:40.330
Where are your friends? Your girlfriend?

00:16:43.370 --> 00:16:45.830
You lonely thing, we're the same.

00:16:45.920 --> 00:16:48.710
We're both to be pitied, poor boy.

00:16:48.790 --> 00:16:51.550
Did you come here just to make fun of me?

00:16:52.050 --> 00:16:54.180
Just you watch! It's my destiny to--

00:16:55.130 --> 00:16:56.590
Do you believe in destiny?

00:16:56.680 --> 00:16:59.010
Oh, well, whatever. Anyway,

00:16:59.100 --> 00:17:02.060
it won't be long
before Shibuya is fixed to this time.

00:17:02.140 --> 00:17:02.980
Fixed?

00:17:03.060 --> 00:17:05.350
Simply put, you won't be able to return.

00:17:06.100 --> 00:17:08.270
That's why I brought my lonely self...

00:17:09.360 --> 00:17:10.980
Daisuke! Are you okay?

00:17:11.280 --> 00:17:12.320
Mr. Kuroiwa!

00:17:12.440 --> 00:17:13.990
When Shibuya is fixed here,

00:17:14.200 --> 00:17:17.070
you'll remain under siege
without hope of rescue.

00:17:17.200 --> 00:17:19.740
If you're going to surrender,
the sooner, the better.

00:17:23.750 --> 00:17:25.750
It looks like
the enemy isn't going to sit idly by.

00:17:26.420 --> 00:17:28.130
I UNDERSTAND. YOU UNDERSTAND ME TOO.

00:17:28.830 --> 00:17:31.210
Well, I guess we can say
you finished writing it.

00:17:32.550 --> 00:17:35.010
But the people of Shibuya
have reached their limit.

00:17:35.630 --> 00:17:37.050
Can't you send some kind of relief?

00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:40.350
<i>Do you intend to destroy the plan
the organization constructed</i>

00:17:40.430 --> 00:17:41.560
<i>due to some fleeting emotion?</i>

00:17:41.640 --> 00:17:44.680
<i>You only exist to realize the future</i>

00:17:44.810 --> 00:17:46.980
<i>told in the prediction.</i>

00:17:47.810 --> 00:17:51.360
<i>Your family and your dead sister
are all expecting that from you.</i>

00:17:51.900 --> 00:17:52.780
<i>Don't you forget that.</i>

00:18:04.870 --> 00:18:09.080
<i>I've gathered together all SDS members
because I made an important decision.</i>

00:18:09.830 --> 00:18:12.040
As you can guess from what that dog said,

00:18:12.500 --> 00:18:13.800
we don't have much time.

00:18:14.380 --> 00:18:16.720
Here's our course of action, I want you

00:18:17.090 --> 00:18:19.930
to attack the Revisions' base.

00:18:20.640 --> 00:18:21.720
Also, I want you to destroy

00:18:22.180 --> 00:18:25.730
the artificial quantum brain that
switched the present and future Shibuya

00:18:26.060 --> 00:18:28.230
and rescue the people who were abducted.

00:18:28.310 --> 00:18:29.350
Are you serious?

00:18:29.440 --> 00:18:31.060
We can go and rescue my mom?

00:18:31.150 --> 00:18:32.690
But the enemy's base...

00:18:32.820 --> 00:18:33.770
What about Milo?

00:18:33.860 --> 00:18:38.070
I don't know about her true feelings,
but I know we can't expect help from AHRV.

00:18:38.150 --> 00:18:39.700
We have to do something ourselves.

00:18:39.780 --> 00:18:41.410
This is going to be dangerous.

00:18:41.490 --> 00:18:42.370
Right.

00:18:42.450 --> 00:18:44.830
However, to resolve this situation,

00:18:45.160 --> 00:18:47.120
I'm asking you to risk your lives.

00:18:48.710 --> 00:18:50.250
-Is this an order?
-No.

00:18:50.540 --> 00:18:51.580
This time,

00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:55.050
I'd like you to decide together.

00:18:55.590 --> 00:18:56.550
I see.

00:18:56.920 --> 00:18:57.920
Then, for this operation,

00:18:58.630 --> 00:18:59.930
I don't want Daisuke involved.

00:19:00.340 --> 00:19:01.390
That's my condition.

00:19:02.050 --> 00:19:03.850
But that will reduce
the strength of your team.

00:19:04.260 --> 00:19:06.220
This operation is different
than anything before.

00:19:07.060 --> 00:19:10.440
If Daisuke acts recklessly,
we could all be in danger.

00:19:10.690 --> 00:19:11.650
I won't take that risk.

00:19:12.560 --> 00:19:14.020
<i>It seems like</i>

00:19:14.150 --> 00:19:17.150
<i>it's your destiny to fight
a petty power struggle like this.</i>

00:19:17.230 --> 00:19:18.690
<i>People's lives depend on this.</i>

00:19:18.820 --> 00:19:20.860
<i>Cut it out, Daisuke.
This is no time for this.</i>

00:19:21.910 --> 00:19:23.320
Fine. Here's what we'll do.

00:19:23.740 --> 00:19:28.580
I want you to tell me whether you think
Daisuke is necessary for this operation.

00:19:28.950 --> 00:19:29.830
You too, Izumi.

00:19:29.910 --> 00:19:32.630
I agree with Gai.

00:19:33.000 --> 00:19:35.840
I believe it's wrong
to break the chain of command.

00:19:36.880 --> 00:19:38.260
I've already given my opinion.

00:19:39.170 --> 00:19:40.050
I...

00:19:43.140 --> 00:19:44.550
want to trust Daisuke again.

00:19:45.600 --> 00:19:48.970
Me too. That makes it two versus two.
Daisuke should come with us.

00:19:49.560 --> 00:19:50.690
Good. Temari.

00:19:50.770 --> 00:19:52.400
Now, I need your opinion.

00:19:52.480 --> 00:19:57.270
I don't know about all this talk
about risking our lives and stuff.

00:19:58.190 --> 00:20:00.110
It wasn't long ago that I was
a normal person.

00:20:00.740 --> 00:20:04.870
<i>We killed people using the String Puppets.
I don't know what's right anymore.</i>

00:20:05.410 --> 00:20:06.740
<i>So, at a time like this,</i>

00:20:07.120 --> 00:20:10.040
<i>if we don't have someone
who can keep their cool, I can't...</i>

00:20:10.710 --> 00:20:14.830
But there's another part of me
that felt secure

00:20:15.290 --> 00:20:17.460
when I heard Daisuke say he'd protect us.

00:20:17.920 --> 00:20:18.750
So...

00:20:21.130 --> 00:20:23.680
So, let's go out there together, Daisuke.

00:20:24.890 --> 00:20:25.760
You bet.

00:20:26.470 --> 00:20:29.180
All right. Let's go
with the majority's decision.

00:20:30.220 --> 00:20:31.390
However...

00:20:31.600 --> 00:20:32.600
this is the last time.

00:22:06.650 --> 00:22:08.110
What? Attack the base?

00:22:08.200 --> 00:22:09.030
<i>Sorry.</i>

00:22:09.200 --> 00:22:11.740
<i>It was my independent decision to
deploy them on this mission.</i>

00:22:12.580 --> 00:22:15.370
It's because the Shibuya people
can no longer wait.

00:22:15.700 --> 00:22:18.080
<i>You sent them out there
without any information or plan?</i>

00:22:18.540 --> 00:22:19.920
<i>They won't make it back alive!</i>

00:22:20.460 --> 00:22:21.960
Don't underestimate the Revisions!

00:22:22.290 --> 00:22:23.500
<i>Yes, that's right.</i>

00:22:23.710 --> 00:22:26.760
<i>I decided without consulting you.</i>

00:22:27.050 --> 00:22:28.430
<i>You won't be responsible for this.</i>

00:22:28.760 --> 00:22:31.720
<i>That's why I want you to tell this
to your commanders</i>

00:22:31.800 --> 00:22:33.390
<i>and get them some help.</i>

00:22:34.600 --> 00:22:37.310
<i>AHRV needs their data, don't they?</i>

00:22:38.850 --> 00:22:39.850
I'm counting on you.

00:22:41.980 --> 00:22:44.820
I'll accept your plan
as the will of the Shibuya people.

00:22:45.900 --> 00:22:46.900
I'll do everything I can.

00:22:50.110 --> 00:22:52.120
Subtitle translation by Brian Athey
